  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "consonant-inventory",
      "number": "15",
      "heading": "The Consonant Letters",
      "statement": "After the vowels come the ব্যঞ্জনবর্ণ (bênjonborno), the consonant letters. Each letter names itself: the consonant sound plus the inherent অ.",
      "examples": [],
      "paradigms": [],
      "footnotes": [
        "The count in the modern inventory is thirty-five once ড়, ঢ় and য় are included; older lists omit those three as separate letters."
      ],
      "seeAlso": [
        "vowel-letters"
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "kind": "grammar",
          "citation": "Wikipedia contributors, \"Bengali alphabet\", *Wikipedia*, retrieved 13 August 2026.",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bengali_alphabet",
          "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      ],
      "core": true
    },
    {
      "id": "five-vargas",
      "number": "16",
      "heading": "The Five Vargas",
      "statement": "Twenty-five of the consonants stand in five rows of five, called বর্গ (bôrgo). Across a row the place of articulation is fixed; down a column the manner changes — unaspirated, aspirated, voiced, voiced-aspirated, nasal.",
      "examples": [],
      "paradigms": [
        {
          "caption": "The five vargas",
          "columns": [
            "unaspirated",
            "aspirated",
            "voiced",
            "voiced asp.",
            "nasal"
          ],
          "rows": [
            {
              "label": "velar",
              "cells": [
                "ক",
                "খ",
                "গ",
                "ঘ",
                "ঙ"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "palatal",
              "cells": [
                "চ",
                "ছ",
                "জ",
                "ঝ",
                "ঞ"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "retroflex",
              "cells": [
                "ট",
                "ঠ",
                "ড",
                "ঢ",
                "ণ"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "dental",
              "cells": [
                "ত",
                "থ",
                "দ",
                "ধ",
                "ন"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "labial",
              "cells": [
                "প",
                "ফ",
                "ব",
                "ভ",
                "ম"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "footnote": "The Sanskrit names of the rows survive in school books: কণ্ঠ্য, তালব্য, মূর্ধন্য, দন্ত্য, ওষ্ঠ্য."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "seeAlso": [
        "consonant-inventory"
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "kind": "grammar",
          "citation": "Wikipedia contributors, \"Bengali alphabet\", *Wikipedia*, retrieved 13 August 2026.",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bengali_alphabet",
          "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      ],
      "core": true
    },
    {
      "id": "final-series",
      "number": "17",
      "heading": "The Final Series",
      "statement": "After the five vargas come য, র, ল, the three sibilants শ ষ স, and হ. These letters do not form a fifth manner-column; they are listed in that fixed order.",
      "examples": [],
      "paradigms": [
        {
          "caption": "Letters after the vargas",
          "columns": [
            "letter",
            "name (Wikipedia)",
            "role"
          ],
          "rows": [
            {
              "label": "য",
              "cells": [
                "yô",
                "affricate at word-start; য-ফলা in conjuncts"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "র",
              "cells": [
                "rô",
                "tap /ɾ/; রেফ and র-ফলা in conjuncts"
              ]
            },
