    },
    {
      "id": "pha-bha-speech",
      "number": "20",
      "heading": "ফ and ভ in Speech",
      "statement": "ফ is written as aspirated প and ভ as aspirated ব. In ordinary speech ফ is often /f/ and ভ often /v/ (or a bilabial fricative), especially in loanwords.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "target": "ফল",
          "roman": "phol",
          "gloss": "fruit"
        },
        {
          "target": "ভালো",
          "roman": "bhalo",
          "gloss": "good"
        }
      ],
